# Emergency guard — copy into ANY web-served folder that ends up holding
# AdRadar code (e.g. public_html, if the app root can't live outside it).
#
# This is a safety net, not the plan: on cPanel the app root belongs
# OUTSIDE public_html, served through "Setup Python App". See
# deploy/CPANEL.md.

# Never serve secrets, the database, or raw source.
<FilesMatch "\.(env|db|sqlite|sqlite3|py|command|json|service|timer|sh|md)$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# .env has a leading dot — FilesMatch above covers it, this is belt-and-braces.
<Files ".env">
  Require all denied
</Files>

# No directory listings (the "Index of /" page).
Options -Indexes
